Synchronize native FAT file operations and both sides of directory moves.

Native C: files commit checked data, archive attributes and timestamps on DOS
flush/close. DOS API wrappers preserve storage errors. Namespace changes sync their parent directories, and rename
invalidates both source and destination caches. USB wrappers retain their
existing stricter per-write commits. Standalone directory mounts retain normal buffering.

